   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You should store the data frame using a reactiveValues object, and use an observeEvent to make the goButton trigger an edit.<div><br></div><div>shinyServer(function(input, output, session) {</div><div>  v &lt;- reactiveValues(data = data.frame(...))</div><div><br></div><div>  output$table &lt;- renderTable({ v$data })</div><div><br></div><div>  observeEvent(input$goButton, {</div><div>    newpatientrow &lt;- ...</div><div>    v$data &lt;- rbind(v$data, newpatientrow)</div><div>  })</div><div>})</div><div><br></div><div>We&#39;ll have a new article on actionButton published on <a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399580708000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Br2QTztlYa_YUu7X98Ner\">shiny.rstudio.com</a> someday soon.</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Mar 24, 2015 at 3:42 PM, Dev Dash <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">pio...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
